WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.336
Hi! Today you describe your day.

2
00:00:06.736 --> 00:00:11.280
What do you do in the morning, at noon and in the evening?

3
00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:15.399
This is my day:

4
00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:18.951
At seven I have breakfast.

5
00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:21.591
Then I shower.

6
00:00:21.991 --> 00:00:25.287
From nine to five I work.

7
00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:28.383
In the evening I read.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:31.671
At eleven I sleep.

9
00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:38.775
Now the golden rule: the verb is in position two.

10
00:00:39.175 --> 00:00:42.063
I have breakfast at seven.

11
00:00:42.463 --> 00:00:45.399
At seven I have breakfast.

12
00:00:45.799 --> 00:00:48.495
In the evening I read.

13
00:00:48.895 --> 00:00:51.135
Then I shower.

14
00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:57.713
Some verbs change their vowel. With ich:

15
00:00:58.113 --> 00:01:00.257
I sleep.

16
00:01:00.657 --> 00:01:03.689
But with du and er, a becomes ä:

17
00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:07.769
You sleep. He sleeps.

18
00:01:08.169 --> 00:01:14.729
The same: fahren, du fährst. And essen, du isst.

19
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:21.001
Listen: Lena asks Mateo about his day.

20
00:01:21.401 --> 00:01:23.737
When do you have breakfast?

21
00:01:24.137 --> 00:01:28.057
At seven. Then I shower.

22
00:01:28.457 --> 00:01:30.889
Do you go by bus?

23
00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:34.081
No, by subway.

24
00:01:34.481 --> 00:01:36.793
And in the evening?

25
00:01:37.193 --> 00:01:39.721
In the evening I read.

26
00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:48.593
Now you! Describe your day. Remember position two!

27
00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.436
Great! Now you can:

28
00:02:02.836 --> 00:02:08.508
You describe your day – and the verb is always in position two.

29
00:02:08.908 --> 00:02:11.028
See you soon!
